1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:04,872
Namaste, and welcome to the complete Hermes
Agent explainer.

2
00:00:04,872 --> 00:00:10,968
Hermes Agent, built by Nous Research, is the
self-improving A I agent with a built-in learning loop.

3
00:00:10,968 --> 00:00:21,804
It creates skills from experience, improves them while you work, reminds itself to save what
matters, searches its own past conversations, and builds a deeper model of you in every session.

4
00:00:21,804 --> 00:00:23,467
Here is the big picture.

5
00:00:23,467 --> 00:00:31,278
You can talk to it from the terminal, or from Telegram, Discord,
Slack, WhatsApp, and Signal, while it actually runs on a cloud machine.

6
00:00:31,278 --> 00:00:38,768
It works with almost any model you choose, from Nous Portal to
OpenRouter and OpenAI, and you can switch models with one command.

7
00:00:38,768 --> 00:00:48,222
In this video, we will unpack the architecture, the learning loop, the platforms, the
automations, and the two-minute quick start, step by step, with tables and diagrams.

8
00:00:48,222 --> 00:00:49,276
Let us begin.

9
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,370
Let us open the hood.

10
00:00:52,370 --> 00:00:53,780
Hermes has three layers.

11
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:55,966
Layer one is the interface layer.

12
00:00:55,966 --> 00:01:08,062
You either type in a full terminal interface, with multi-line editing, slash commands, history,
and streaming tool output, or you message it from chat apps through a single gateway process.

13
00:01:08,062 --> 00:01:10,779
Layer two is the agent runtime.

14
00:01:10,779 --> 00:01:12,107
This is the brain.

15
00:01:12,107 --> 00:01:23,860
It runs the conversation loop, calls more than forty tools, delegates work to isolated
sub-agents, compresses old context so long sessions never break, and tracks usage and cost.

16
00:01:23,860 --> 00:01:26,179
Layer three is the state layer.

17
00:01:26,179 --> 00:01:34,522
Every session, message, and memory is stored in a local database with
full-text search, so the agent can recall anything across sessions.

18
00:01:34,522 --> 00:01:35,885
Follow one message.

19
00:01:35,885 --> 00:01:37,734
You send a text on Telegram.

20
00:01:37,734 --> 00:01:46,794
The gateway routes it to your session, the runtime thinks, calls
tools, and replies, and the state layer saves everything for next time.

21
00:01:46,794 --> 00:01:49,144
One brain, many doors, total memory.

22
00:01:50,670 --> 00:01:56,503
This is the heart of Hermes, the closed
learning loop, and it has five moving parts.

23
00:01:56,503 --> 00:01:59,187
Part one, agent-curated memory with periodic
nudges.

24
00:01:59,187 --> 00:02:06,518
The agent itself decides what is worth remembering, and the
system nudges it to persist knowledge before it is lost.

25
00:02:06,518 --> 00:02:09,400
Part two, autonomous skill creation.

26
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:16,249
After a complex task, Hermes writes a reusable skill from what
it just learned, so it never solves the same problem twice.

27
00:02:16,249 --> 00:02:19,686
Part three, skills that self-improve during
use.

28
00:02:19,686 --> 00:02:22,639
Every time a skill runs, the agent refines
it.

29
00:02:22,639 --> 00:02:25,597
Part four, session search with
summarisation.

30
00:02:25,597 --> 00:02:31,034
Full-text search finds old conversations, and the
model summarises them for cross-session recall.

31
00:02:31,034 --> 00:02:40,307
Part five, a deepening model of you, powered by Honcho, an open-source
user-modelling system, plus compatibility with the open agentskills dot io standard.

32
00:02:40,307 --> 00:02:43,903
Memory writes, skills learn, recall
compounds.

33
00:02:43,903 --> 00:02:47,094
That is why Hermes gets smarter the longer
you use it.

34
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:52,099
Hermes lives where you do, and runs where
you want.

35
00:02:52,099 --> 00:02:53,771
First, where you talk.

36
00:02:53,771 --> 00:02:59,565
One gateway process serves Telegram, Discord, Slack,
WhatsApp, Signal, and the command line together.

37
00:02:59,565 --> 00:03:06,177
It transcribes your voice memos, and your conversation
continues seamlessly even if you switch apps.

38
00:03:06,177 --> 00:03:06,677
Now, where it runs.

39
00:03:06,677 --> 00:03:09,269
Hermes has seven terminal backends.

40
00:03:09,269 --> 00:03:17,776
Local for your own machine, Docker and SSH for servers, Singularity
for clusters, and Modal, Daytona, and Vercel Sandbox for the cloud.

41
00:03:17,776 --> 00:03:19,982
The serverless options are special.

42
00:03:19,982 --> 00:03:26,774
Your agent's environment hibernates when idle and wakes
on demand, so it costs almost nothing between sessions.

43
00:03:26,774 --> 00:03:32,975
That means one setup choice covers everything,
from a five-dollar V P S to a full G P U cluster.

44
00:03:32,975 --> 00:03:35,736
Chat from your phone, compute in the cloud.

45
00:03:37,230 --> 00:03:39,008
Now the power features.

46
00:03:39,008 --> 00:03:41,880
Delegation, automation, and research.

47
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:42,380
Delegation first.

48
00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:48,650
Hermes can spawn isolated sub-agents for parallel
workstreams, so three tasks finish in the time of one.

49
00:03:48,650 --> 00:03:58,682
It can also write Python scripts that call its own tools through R P C, collapsing
long multi-step pipelines into a single step that costs almost zero context.

50
00:03:58,682 --> 00:04:00,099
Automation next.

51
00:04:00,099 --> 00:04:10,691
A built-in cron scheduler takes plain-English schedules, like a daily report, a nightly
backup, or a weekly audit, and delivers the result to any platform, fully unattended.

52
00:04:10,691 --> 00:04:12,076
Finally, research.

53
00:04:12,076 --> 00:04:21,116
Hermes supports batch trajectory generation and trajectory compression,
producing training data for the next generation of tool-calling models.

54
00:04:21,116 --> 00:04:25,364
Parallel workers, scheduled habits, and a
data flywheel for researchers.

55
00:04:25,364 --> 00:04:26,886
Let us get you installed.

56
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:37,329
On Linux, macOS, W S L two, or Termux, you run one install command from the
Hermes docs site, then reload your shell and type hermes to start chatting.

57
00:04:37,329 --> 00:04:44,365
On Windows, there is a native PowerShell installer that
bundles everything, including Python, Node, and a portable Git.

58
00:04:44,365 --> 00:04:46,789
Day to day, you need only a few commands.

59
00:04:46,789 --> 00:04:56,723
Hermes model to switch providers, hermes gateway to start messaging, hermes setup for
the full wizard, hermes update to upgrade, and hermes doctor to diagnose problems.

60
00:04:56,723 --> 00:04:58,257
Want to skip collecting five A P I keys?

61
00:04:58,257 --> 00:05:00,681
Run hermes setup with the portal flag.

62
00:05:00,681 --> 00:05:11,000
One Nous Portal subscription gives you three hundred plus models, plus web
search, image generation, speech, and a cloud browser through the Tool Gateway.

63
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,724
Full docs are on the Hermes site, and the
community lives on Discord.

64
00:05:14,724 --> 00:05:18,128
Thank you for watching, and happy building
with Hermes Agent.
